From: teo-casares <gist 8b64949638e1952602a7f435bb34d5b8>
Subject: [PATCH] 8250_mtk: honour _DSD clock-frequency / NVDA0240 52 MHz clock

The ACPI path of 8250_mtk hardcodes a 26 MHz UART clock, but the NVIDIA
N1X/GB10 SAM EC UART (NVDA0240) actually runs at ~52 MHz, so the link
came up at ~8 Mbaud and the EC ignored it. Honours the _DSD
"clock-frequency" property, else 52 MHz.

Compile-safe against vanilla 7.3.1: uses device_property_read_u32 only
(no acpi.h symbols — acpi_dev_hid_match/ACPI_COMPANION are not available
in 8250_mtk.c's include set there). Mutually exclusive with the
surface_aggregator baud-halving quirk (0002) — enable only one.

STAGED ONLY upstream (not built/installed by teo-casares): 8250_mtk is
built-in (=y). Evidence: raw MMIO sweep on COM3 (NVDA0240:01) shows the
SAM EC replies cleanly only at 12.3..13.3 UART clocks/bit for its
4,000,000-baud link => real UART input clock ~52 MHz.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_mtk.c
@@ -240,3 +240,12 @@ static int mtk8250_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	uart.port.uartclk = clk_get_rate(data->uart_clk);
-	if (!uart.port.uartclk)
-		uart.port.uartclk = 26 * HZ_PER_MHZ;
+	if (!uart.port.uartclk) {
+		u32 freq;
+		/*
+		 * ACPI: honour _DSD "clock-frequency"; NVIDIA N1X/GB10 UARTs run at
+		 * 52 MHz. device_property_read_u32 needs no acpi.h symbols.
+		 */
+		if (!device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "clock-frequency", &freq) && freq)
+			uart.port.uartclk = freq;
+		else
+			uart.port.uartclk = 52 * HZ_PER_MHZ;
+	}
